  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-26T17:05:33.644Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For when a VRC_station wouldn't work, or TeleportTo is too buggy to do continuously.\n\nIf the entire reason for it missing is that it could be used maliciously, then TeleportTo can accomplish the same, it just has a bug that causes a single frame hitch when you look too far up or down (at almost precisely 30 degrees and 330 degrees), other than that it seems to work fine, excluding that it might be sending out tons of network traffic.\n\nI propose that to fix any malicious use the function could just be disabled whenever the menu is open and it would be better than what we have now as I have gotten myself stuck rotating at speed with TeleportTo.\n\nMy reason for asking is that there is a flight script (flap arms, you fly) that tried to implement banking (twist body, you turn in that direction), but because of the mentioned TeleportTo bug, and that it might be flooding the network, it isn't ideal.",
